    "note": "Own number of the paper ('our RBM+PP wave function with 6 × 6 sublattice structure gives a better precision of ...'). C1: Eq. (1) H = J1 sum Si·Sj + J2 sum Si·Sj, spin-1/2, J1 = 1, each bond once, no constant: Pauli total = 4N x E/N. C3: 18 x 18, 'the periodic boundary condition is assumed' (Sec. III A). C4: S = 0, K = (0,0) is the ground-state sector; momentum and spin-parity projections always applied (App. A). C5: J2 = 0.5. Variational (VMC of a projected RBM+PP state; no Lanczos step, no extrapolation); sampled and carries its own sigma; below it on this instance sits only the sigma-less CNN1 + 1 Lanczos step -0.49651 of Liang et al. The (3) is not defined in the text. method_detail 'point group (simplified)' is an inference: App. A states the simplified point-group projection for the optimized S = 0, K = (0,0) ground state used for correlation functions and for the Fig. 10 energies, not explicitly for the note [73] energy. No duplicate: the instance's other rows are Hu et al. p = 0, p = 1 (-0.49611(1), quoted in the same note but carried from its primary), the p -> 0-variance extrapolation, Li et al. CNN and Liang et al. CNN1; Liang et al. (arXiv:2204.07816v1 text) quote '-0.496275 reported in [33]' and that quote is not a row. Versions: the note and its -0.496275(3) are identical in the TeX of v5 (13 Jun 2021) and v6 (12 Jul 2021, post-acceptance); v1 has no 18 x 18 data and v3 no such note (v2, v4 not fetched). Journal PRX 11, 031034 not read (journals.aps.org 403 to node fetch). peer_reviewed true (PRX).",
